terms.medium_def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Sa.25.3; 
only referred to as Nabal (נָבָל); 
husband of Abigail. § a man of Carmel who spurned David's messengers, then died of shock when he realised it might cause his death; his case was pleaded by his wife Abigail who became David's wife after his death
